Root cause:
The bug was caused by the `UnsynchronizedBuffer.Reader` class not correctly handling `ByteBuffer` instances that do not start at position 0. Specifically, the original implementation only checked if the `ByteBuffer` had an underlying array but did not account for the case where the `ByteBuffer`'s position was not at the start of the array. This led to incorrect calculations of the offset, resulting in potential `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` when reading from the buffer. The patch fixed this by adjusting the offset calculation to include the current position of the `ByteBuffer`, ensuring that data is read correctly from the intended starting point.
